{
  "id": "note-update-delete",
  "title": "updateNote writes exactly the registers the body names; deleteNote hides the note and its cards, twice is 204; a deleted note is 410",
  "covers": [
    "notes.update_registers",
    "notes.update_validation",
    "notes.update_rematch",
    "notes.delete",
    "notes.delete_twice",
    "notes.deleted_410"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "Two vocab notes, each with a new meaning card: note ...01 (entry 1001010) and note ...02 (entry 1001150).",
    "Step 0 sets two fields. Step 1 clears one with the empty string; the other keeps its value (a partial map: only the keys present are written).",
    "Step 2 adds two tags (the answer's tags are sorted ascending). Step 3 removes one; a tag that is not on the note is ignored. Step 4 replaces the whole set (duplicates collapse). Step 5 sets the mnemonic; the tags are untouched.",
    "Step 6 sets source_sentence alone: the one register covers all three members, so the ids not sent are null. Step 7 reads the note back: every edit is there and the note still has its card.",
    "Steps 8-10 are 422 validation_failed and mint nothing: tags together with add_tags, an empty body, an immutable property.",
    "Step 11: the note is unchanged by the refused requests (same updated_at as step 7).",
    "Step 12 re-matches note ...02 to an entry no other live note holds (1001580): no collision, so no merge (the collision is a documented difference, SHELL.md 4.3, and is not parity-tested; neither is a re-match to an entry that is in no dictionary: the server accepts it with 200 while SHELL.md 4.3 has the shell check it like createNote, an open contract question).",
    "Steps 13-14: an id that exists nowhere is 404 for update and for delete.",
    "Step 15 deletes note ...01: 204. Step 16 deletes it again: 204, nothing minted.",
    "Step 17: reading it is 410 gone; step 18: with include_deleted=true it is 200 with its last content. Step 19: updating it is 410 gone.",
    "Step 20: its card is hidden through the note's tombstone (410 gone); step 21: with include_deleted=true the card is returned and its own deleted_at is null (no card.deleted is minted).",
    "Step 22: the queue serves only the card of note ...02."
  ],
